# --- Public panel tunnel (referenced/tunnel.py) -----------------------------
# The public link is a cloudflared QUICK tunnel: free, no Cloudflare account, no
# domain, and nothing between the browser and the panel. Its address is random
# and changes on restart, but jamesheston.pages.dev/dashboard always redirects to
# the current one, so that is the link to share.
#
# localtunnel is the fallback. Its address is stable (<name>.loca.lt), but the
# loca.lt service shows browsers an HTTP 511 "Tunnel website ahead" page before
# forwarding them, so it is a worse link to hand to anybody.
#
# Note: an already-set environment variable beats .env (python-dotenv never
# overwrites one), so if TUNNEL_PROVIDER is exported in the shell, a systemd
# unit or a start script, this file's value is ignored and the startup log says
# so. Clear it there to let .env decide.
#
# DASHBOARD_TUNNEL=0                             turn the tunnel off entirely
# TUNNEL_PROVIDER=cloudflared                    the default, or 'localtunnel' first
# CLOUDFLARED_PATH=                              exact path to the cloudflared
#                                                binary, when it is installed
#                                                somewhere the search misses
# LOCALTUNNEL_SUBDOMAIN=jamesheston              the name in <name>.loca.lt
# LOCALTUNNEL_ATTEMPTS=3                         tries before giving up on localtunnel
# LOCALTUNNEL_PORT=                              tunnel a port other than 5000
# CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_PROTOCOL=http2               only if a quick tunnel connects
#                                                but never answers (blocks UDP 7844)
#
# Named cloudflared tunnel. Needs a domain on Cloudflare whose hostname routes to
# the tunnel; without one it answers nothing. Leave CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_MODE unset
# to stay on quick tunnels.
# CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_MODE=named
# CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=
# CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_URL=https://panel.example.com
